#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:261
msgid "References"
msgstr "Referencias"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:262
msgid ""
"References work by calling any \"target\"- either tags (titles, headings, "
"figures, and tables) or labels (equations). These reference formats work "
"internally- calling something within the same document and externally- "
"calling content in some other document within this same project."
msgstr ""
"Las referencias funcionan llamando a cualquier \"destino\": ya sea etiquetas"
" (títulos, encabezados, figuras y tablas) o etiquetas (ecuaciones). Estos "
"formatos de referencia funcionan internamente: llamando a algo dentro del "
"mismo documento y externamente, llamando contenido en otro documento dentro "
"de ese mismo proyecto."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:264
msgid ""
"Before you start tagging and labelling content with any degree of willy-"
"nilly-ness, make sure that you are not repeating tags or labels. You can "
"check to see if your tag or label is taken by visiting libraries on GitHub. "
":download:`Check here for tags and labels: "
"</_static/text_documents/heading_index.txt>`."
msgstr ""
"Antes de empezar a etiquetar y etiquetar contenido con cualquier grado de "
"desorden, asegúrate de no estar repitiendo etiquetas o etiquetas. Puedes "
"comprobar si tu etiqueta o etiqueta está tomada visitando bibliotecas en "
"GitHub. :download:`Check here for tags and labels: "
"</_static/text_documents/heading_index.txt>`."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:267
msgid "Document Titles and Headings"
msgstr "Títulos y encabezamientos de documentos"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:268
msgid ""
"This content should be called with the ``:ref:`tag``` functionality. You can"
" also choose what text will be shown. For example, ``:ref:`This text "
"<heading_links_and_references>``` gives :ref:`This text "
"<heading_links_and_references>`."
msgstr ""
"This content should be called with the ``:ref:`tag``` functionality. You can"
" also choose what text will be shown. For example, ``:ref:`This text "
"<heading_links_and_references>``` gives :ref:`This text "
